From 993781ed7bfbefcb11ebead503209fc65da3ad6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grzegorz Gajoch <gajoch@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:36:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(wifi): USB WiFi dongles in host mode

- Linux: cfg80211, mac80211, ath9k_htc (AR9271) and mt7601u. Their firmware
  and regulatory.db are built into the kernel from board/ulanzi/d200/firmware
  (with their licences): in host mode USB devices probe before the root
  filesystem is mounted. The unsigned regdb is accepted (EXPERT,
  CFG80211_CERTIFICATION_ONUS), which keeps X.509 and OpenSSL out of the
  kernel build.
- wpa_supplicant (nl80211, wpa_cli) and iw.
- S32wifi: once wlan0 appears, wpa_supplicant with /data/wpa_supplicant.conf,
  then udhcpc.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
